{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>A nevelah and a terefah he shall not eat, to become impure by it.</b> Here He warns concerning impurity — that if he ate a nevelah of a clean bird, which has no impurity of contact or carrying but only impurity of eating in the digestive tract, it is forbidden to eat of consecrated things; and he must say ״וּטְרֵפָה״ — that which has a terefah in its species, excluding the nevelah of an unclean bird which has no terefah in its species."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:41.446300931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}